  <completion-notes date="2026-07-08" model="opus" rigor="FULL">
    <summary>
      CreateMatterWizard was ALREADY refactored (before this project) into a thin
      wrapper around the shared CreateRecordWizard. Its Next-Steps card grid and
      Send-Email step render through CreateRecordWizard (task 021's domain, now
      backed by the shared WizardFollowOns module) — NOT through the local
      NextStepsStep.tsx / SendEmailStep.tsx. Those two local files were orphaned
      DEAD DUPLICATES: their exported symbols (NextStepsStep, FollowOnActionId,
      IFollowOnCardDef, INextStepsStepProps, FOLLOW_ON_STEP_ID_MAP,
      FOLLOW_ON_STEP_LABEL_MAP, SendEmailStep, ISendEmailStepProps) were referenced
      only within their own files. The single live cross-reference was the barrel
      re-exporting two unused helpers (buildDefaultEmailSubject / buildDefaultEmailBody)
      from ./SendEmailStep — grep-verified to have zero consumers (CreateMatterWizard.tsx
      builds its email subject/body inline via the CreateRecordWizard config;
      the LegalWorkspace solution has its own separate CreateMatter copies).

      Therefore step 1's "swap the local NextStepsStep for a FollowOnGrid +
      FollowOnCardConfig[]" reduced to pure deletion. Authoring a FollowOnCardConfig[]
      inside CreateMatterWizard would be dead code (nothing renders it; the grid is
      owned by CreateRecordWizard/task 021) and would violate CLAUDE.md §11
      (Component Justification — no unreferenced new surface). Not an ADR conflict;
      surfaced here per §6.5 as a task-premise mismatch resolved by doing the correct
      minimal thing that satisfies all three acceptance criteria.
    </summary>
    <changes>
      <file action="deleted">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateMatterWizard/NextStepsStep.tsx (orphaned dead duplicate — never imported by CreateMatterWizard.tsx)</file>
      <file action="deleted">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateMatterWizard/SendEmailStep.tsx (orphaned dead duplicate)</file>
      <file action="edited">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateMatterWizard/index.ts (removed the unused buildDefaultEmailSubject/buildDefaultEmailBody re-export from ./SendEmailStep; added a rationale comment)</file>
      <file action="edited">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateMatterWizard/matterService.ts (updated one stale comment referencing SendEmailStep -> "Send Email follow-on"; no logic change)</file>
    </changes>
    <scope-safety>Touched ONLY files inside CreateMatterWizard/. Did NOT touch CreateRecordWizard/, CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/, SummarizeFilesWizard/, WizardFollowOns/, or src/components/index.ts (sibling tasks 021/023/024 own those). Did NOT edit TASK-INDEX.md or current-task.md (orchestrator-owned).</scope-safety>
    <acceptance>
      <criterion status="pass">Grep for NextStepsStep|SendEmailStep in CreateMatterWizard/ returns only comment lines — no source files, no imports.</criterion>
      <criterion status="pass">Regression: Matter creation + follow-ons unchanged. Card set + follow-on creation are driven by CreateRecordWizard config (selectedActions: assign-counsel / create-event / send-email) and CreateMatterWizard.onFinish (MatterService.createMatter, WorkAssignmentService, EventService, associateToRecord). None of these paths imported the deleted files, so deletion is behavior-neutral by construction.</criterion>
      <criterion status="pass">Shared lib builds: `npm run build` (tsc) clean.</criterion>
    </acceptance>
    <verification>
      <item>Build: `npm run build` (@spaarke/ui-components@2.3.0, tsc) — 0 errors.</item>
      <item>Tests: `npx jest CreateMatterWizard` — matterService.cascade.test.ts, 5/5 pass.</item>
      <item>Quality gates: code-review (no Critical/Warning; deletion improves quality direction) + adr-check (Compliant: ADR-012/021/028; no violations; §10/§11 do not fire) — both PASS.</item>
    </verification>
  </completion-notes>
</task>
